um validation","additionalProperties:false","Timeout","Authorization check"],"correct":1},{"q":"Why are validation, coercion, authorization, and sandboxing treated as distinct concerns?","qKn":"Validation, coercion, authorization, sandboxing ಅನ್ನೂ ಏಕೆ ಪ್ರತ್ಯೇಕ ಕಾಳಜಿಗಳೆಂದೂ ಪರಿಗಣಿಸಲಾಗುತ್ತದೆ?","opts":["They are actually the same thing","A tool that passes validation can still be unauthorized or unsandboxed, so conflating them causes security bugs","Only coercion matters in practice","Sandboxing is never needed"],"optsKn":["ಅವೂ ಅಸಲಿಗೆ ಒಂದೇ","Validation ಪಾಸ್ ಆದ tool ಇನ್ನೂ unauthorized ಅಥವಾ unsandboxed ಆಗಿರಬಹುದು","Coercion ಮಾತ್ರ ಪ್ರಾಯೋಗಿಕವಾಗಿ ಮುಖ್ಯ","Sandboxing ಎಂದಿಗೂ ಅಗತ್ಯ ಇಲ್ಲ"],"correct":1}]}},{"type":"concept","data":{"headingEn":"Key Takeaways","headingKn":"ಮುಖ್ಯ ಅಂಶಗಳು","bodyEn":"• Validation, coercion, authorization, and sandboxing are four distinct checks, not one.
• Coercion should be narrow and deterministic — convert only unambiguous representations.
• additionalProperties:false turns silently-passed extra fields into caught validation errors.
• A structured error taxonomy (unknown_tool/validation_error/execution_error/timeout) lets the model self-correct.","bodyKn":"• Validation, coercion, authorization, sandboxing ನಾಲ್ಕೂ ಪ್ರತ್ಯೇಕ ಪರಿಶೋಧನೆಗಳು.
• Coercion ಕಿರಿದಾಗಿ ಮತ್ತು deterministic ಆಗಿರಬೇಕು.
